# Cost-Aware Program.cs Template

When scaffolding or reviewing `Program.cs`, follow this pattern:

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Diagnostics;

var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

// Telemetry safeguard
builder.Logging.AddFilter("Microsoft", LogLevel.Warning);
builder.Logging.AddFilter("System", LogLevel.Warning);
builder.Logging.AddFilter("juskel", LogLevel.Information);

builder.Services.AddOpenApi();
builder.Services.AddProblemDetails();
builder.Services.AddExceptionHandler<GlobalExceptionHandler>();
builder.Services.AddHealthChecks(); // in-memory only — no DB

var app = builder.Build();

if (app.Environment.IsDevelopment())
    app.MapOpenApi();

app.UseExceptionHandler();
app.MapHealthChecks("/health");
app.MapGet("/", () => Results.Ok(new { status = "Online", version = "1.0.0" }));

app.Run();
```

`GlobalExceptionHandler` must implement `IExceptionHandler` and return `ProblemDetails` JSON.
